// பாடம் 2: தமிழோவியம் (கவிதைப் பேழை - ஈரோடு தமிழன்பன்) [Q029 - Q056]
// 'காலம் பிறக்கும் முன் பிறந்தது தமிழே', ஹைக்கூ, சென்ரியூ, லிமரைக்கூ, 'வணக்கம் வள்ளுவ' சாகித்திய அகாதெமி (2004), கவிதைத் தொகுப்புகள், அறிவியல் பார்வை
// ==============================================================================
{"id": "9th-u1-q029", "schema_version": "1.0", "kind": "statement_analysis", "level": "SSLC", "difficulty": "medium", "exam_mappings": ["group_4", "group_2", "group_2a"], "syllabus": {"class": "9", "subject_id": "general_tamil", "term": "full_year", "unit_id": "ta-9th-u1-mozhi", "lesson_id": "lesson-01-dravida-mozhi-kudumbam", "chapter_id": null, "topic_id": "topic-dravida-idam-peyargal", "subtopic_id": null}, "texts": {"ta": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "திராவிட மொழிகளின் இடப்பெயர்கள் (Pronouns) குறித்த பின்வரும் கூற்றுகளை ஆராய்க:\n1. திராவிட மொழிகளில் தன்மை, முன்னிலை, படர்க்கை ஆகிய மூவிடப் பெயர்களிலும் பொதுவான ஒற்றுமை காணப்படுகிறது.\n2. தமிழின் 'நான்' என்ற தன்மை ஒருமைப் பெயர் மலையாளத்தில் 'ஞான்' என்றும், தெலுங்கில் 'நேனு' என்றும் கன்னடத்தில் 'நானு' என்றும் வழங்குகிறது.\n3. வடமொழியில் உள்ளவாறே திராவிட மொழிகளிலும் மூவிடப் பெயர்கள் உருமாற்றம் அடைந்துள்ளன.\nமேற்கண்ட கூற்றுகளுள் சரியானவை எவை?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "1, 2 மட்டும் சரி", "B": "2, 3 மட்டும் சரி", "C": "1, 3 மட்டும் சரி", "D": "அனைத்தும் சரி"}, "explanation": "திராவிட மொழிகளின் மூவிடப் பெயர்கள் ஒன்றுக்கொன்று நெருங்கிய தொடர்புடையவை. வடமொழியோடு இவற்றுக்குத் தொடர்பில்லை (கூற்று 3 தவறு). 1 மற்றும் 2 சரியானவை."}, "en": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "Analyze the statements regarding pronouns in Dravidian languages:\n1. Dravidian languages display remarkable structural uniformity across first, second, and third person pronouns.\n2. The Tamil first person singular 'Naan' appears as 'Njaan' in Malayalam, 'Nenu' in Telugu, and 'Naanu' in Kannada.\n3. Pronouns in Dravidian languages underwent phonetic evolution identically to Indo-Aryan tongues.\nWhich statements are correct?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "1 and 2 only are correct", "B": "2 and 3 only are correct", "C": "1 and 3 only are correct", "D": "All are correct"}, "explanation": "Dravidian personal pronouns are native and strictly independent of Sanskrit paradigms. Statements 1 and 2 are correct."}}, "question_data": {"assertion": null, "reason": null, "statements": [], "matching_pairs": [], "ordered_items": [], "numeric_answer": null, "passage_reference": null, "table_reference": null, "image_reference": null}, "answer": {"correct_key": "A", "accepted_keys": ["A"], "correct_order": [], "matching_answer": [], "numeric_value": null, "explanation_key": null}, "question_settings": {"is_negative_question": false, "marks": 1.5, "negative_marks": 0.0, "allow_multiple_answers": false}, "source": {"type": "book", "book_name": "Tamil Nadu Samacheer Kalvi", "publisher": "Tamil Nadu Textbook and Educational Services Corporation", "class": "9", "term": "full_year", "edition": "2024-2025", "page": 7, "chapter": null, "section": null, "reference": "9th Tamil, Unit 1, Page 7", "url": null, "source_notes": null}, "previous_year": {"is_previous_year": false, "exam": null, "exam_name": null, "year": null, "paper": null, "session": null}, "media": {"has_media": false, "items": []}, "tags": ["dravidian_pronouns", "comparative_linguistics", "statement_analysis"], "language_status": {"ta": "available", "en": "available"}, "workflow": {"status": "published", "verification_status": "verified", "created_by": "admin", "created_at": "2026-11-04T09:50:00Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-04T09:50:00Z"}, "version": {"current": 1, "previous_version_id": null, "revision_reason": null}}
{"id": "9th-u1-q030", "schema_version": "1.0", "kind": "matching", "level": "SSLC", "difficulty": "medium", "exam_mappings": ["group_4", "group_2", "group_2a"], "syllabus": {"class": "9", "subject_id": "general_tamil", "term": "full_year", "unit_id": "ta-9th-u1-mozhi", "lesson_id": "lesson-01-dravida-mozhi-kudumbam", "chapter_id": null, "topic_id": "topic-pronoun-cognates", "subtopic_id": null}, "texts": {"ta": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "தமிழ்த்தன்மை ஒருமைப் பெயரான 'யான் / நான்' பிற திராவிட மொழிகளில் மருவியுள்ள வடிவங்களைப் பொருத்துக:\nபட்டியல் I:\na) மலையாளம்\nb) தெலுங்கு\nc) கன்னடம்\nd) துளு\n\nபட்டியல் II:\n1. யானு / ஏனு\n2. நேனு\n3. ஞான்\n4. நானு", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "a-2, b-3, c-4, d-1", "B": "a-3, b-2, c-4, d-1", "C": "a-3, b-4, c-2, d-1", "D": "a-4, b-2, c-1, d-3"}, "explanation": "நான்: மலையாளம் = ஞான் (3); தெலுங்கு = நேனு (2); கன்னடம் = நானு (4); துளு = யானு/ஏனு (1). சரியான வரிசை: 3, 2, 4, 1."}, "en": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "Match the Dravidian tongues with their cognate forms of the first-person singular pronoun 'I' (நான்):\nList I: a) Malayalam, b) Telugu, c) Kannada, d) Tulu\nList II: 1. Yaanu / Eenu, 2. Nenu, 3. Njaan, 4. Naanu", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "a-2, b-3, c-4, d-1", "B": "a-3, b-2, c-4, d-1", "C": "a-3, b-4, c-2, d-1", "D": "a-4, b-2, c-1, d-3"}, "explanation": "Malayalam: Njaan (3); Telugu: Nenu (2); Kannada: Naanu (4); Tulu: Yaanu (1). Sequence: 3, 2, 4, 1."}}, "question_data": {"assertion": null, "reason": null, "statements": [], "matching_pairs": [], "ordered_items": [], "numeric_answer": null, "passage_reference": null, "table_reference": null, "image_reference": null}, "answer": {"correct_key": "B", "accepted_keys": ["B"], "correct_order": [], "matching_answer": [], "numeric_value": null, "explanation_key": null}, "question_settings": {"is_negative_question": false, "marks": 1.5, "negative_marks": 0.0, "allow_multiple_answers": false}, "source": {"type": "book", "book_name": "Tamil Nadu Samacheer Kalvi", "publisher": "Tamil Nadu Textbook and Educational Services Corporation", "class": "9", "term": "full_year", "edition": "2024-2025", "page": 7, "chapter": null, "section": null, "reference": "9th Tamil, Unit 1, Page 7", "url": null, "source_notes": null}, "previous_year": {"is_previous_year": false, "exam": null, "exam_name": null, "year": null, "paper": null, "session": null}, "media": {"has_media": false, "items": []}, "tags": ["pronouns", "matching", "dravidian_cognates"], "language_status": {"ta": "available", "en": "available"}, "workflow": {"status": "published", "verification_status": "verified", "created_by": "admin", "created_at": "2026-11-04T09:50:00Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-04T09:50:00Z"}, "version": {"current": 1, "previous_version_id": null, "revision_reason": null}}
{"id": "9th-u1-q031", "schema_version": "1.0", "kind": "direct", "level": "SSLC", "difficulty": "easy", "exam_mappings": ["group_4", "group_2", "group_2a"], "syllabus": {"class": "9", "subject_id": "general_tamil", "term": "full_year", "unit_id": "ta-9th-u1-mozhi", "lesson_id": "lesson-01-dravida-mozhi-kudumbam", "chapter_id": null, "topic_id": "topic-maram-cognates", "subtopic_id": null}, "texts": {"ta": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "'மரம்' என்ற தமிழ்ச் சொல் தெலுங்கு மொழியில் எவ்வாறு வழங்கப்படுகிறது?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "மரம்", "B": "மர", "C": "மானு / செட்டு", "D": "மரனு"}, "explanation": "திராவிட அடிச்சொல் ஆய்வில்: மரம் (தமிழ், மலையாளம்), மர (கன்னடம்), மானு (தெலுங்கு)."}, "en": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "In comparative Dravidian linguistics, what is the Telugu cognate for the Tamil root word 'Maram' (Tree)?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "Maram", "B": "Mara", "C": "Maanu", "D": "Maranu"}, "explanation": "Tamil & Malayalam use 'Maram'; Kannada uses 'Mara'; Telugu uses 'Maanu' (and Chettu)."}}, "question_data": {"assertion": null, "reason": null, "statements": [], "matching_pairs": [], "ordered_items": [], "numeric_answer": null, "passage_reference": null, "table_reference": null, "image_reference": null}, "answer": {"correct_key": "C", "accepted_keys": ["C"], "correct_order": [], "matching_answer": [], "numeric_value": null, "explanation_key": null}, "question_settings": {"is_negative_question": false, "marks": 1.5, "negative_marks": 0.0, "allow_multiple_answers": false}, "source": {"type": "book", "book_name": "Tamil Nadu Samacheer Kalvi", "publisher": "Tamil Nadu Textbook and Educational Services Corporation", "class": "9", "term": "full_year", "edition": "2024-2025", "page": 6, "chapter": null, "section": null, "reference": "9th Tamil, Unit 1, Page 6", "url": null, "source_notes": null}, "previous_year": {"is_previous_year": false, "exam": null, "exam_name": null, "year": null, "paper": null, "session": null}, "media": {"has_media": false, "items": []}, "tags": ["etymology", "tree_cognates", "direct_mcq"], "language_status": {"ta": "available", "en": "available"}, "workflow": {"status": "published", "verification_status": "verified", "created_by": "admin", "created_at": "2026-11-04T09:50:00Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-04T09:50:00Z"}, "version": {"current": 1, "previous_version_id": null, "revision_reason": null}}
{"id": "9th-u1-q032", "schema_version": "1.0", "kind": "statement_analysis", "level": "SSLC", "difficulty": "hard", "exam_mappings": ["group_4", "group_2", "group_2a"], "syllabus": {"class": "9", "subject_id": "general_tamil", "term": "full_year", "unit_id": "ta-9th-u1-mozhi", "lesson_id": "lesson-01-dravida-mozhi-kudumbam", "chapter_id": null, "topic_id": "topic-dravida-adjectives", "subtopic_id": null}, "texts": {"ta": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "திராவிட மொழிகளின் பெயரடைகள் (Adjectives) குறித்த பின்வரும் கூற்றுகளை ஆராய்க:\n1. திராவிட மொழிகளில் பெயரடைகளும் வினையடைகளும் தமக்குரிய சொல்லுக்கு முன்னரே வருகின்றன.\n2. வடமொழியில் உள்ளவாறு பெயரடைகள் பால், எண், திணைக்கு ஏற்ப உருமாற்றம் அடைவதில்லை; திராவிடத்தில் பெயரடைகள் மாறாமல் அப்படியே நிற்கும்.\n3. 'நல்ல பெண்', 'நல்ல பையன்' என்பதில் 'நல்ல' என்னும் பெயரடை பாலிற்கு ஏற்ப மாறாமல் நிற்பதே திராவிட மொழிகளின் தனிச்சிறப்பாகும்.\nமேற்கண்ட கூற்றுகளுள் சரியானவை எவை?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "1, 2 மட்டும்", "B": "2, 3 மட்டும்", "C": "1, 3 மட்டும்", "D": "அனைத்தும் சரி"}, "explanation": "கால்டுவெல் குறிப்பிட்டவாறு: திராவிட மொழிகளில் பெயரடைகள் பாலிற்கு ஏற்ப மாறுவதில்லை (வடமொழியில் சுந்தர: புருஷ:, சுந்தரீ ஸ்த்ரீ என மாறும்). எனவே மூன்று கூற்றுகளும் முற்றிலும் சரியானவை."}, "en": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "Analyze the following statements regarding Adjectives in Dravidian languages:\n1. In Dravidian languages, both adjectives and adverbs precede the words they qualify.\n2. Unlike Indo-Aryan languages, Dravidian adjectives do not change their morphological endings according to gender, number, or case.\n3. For example, 'Nalla' (good) remains unchanged in both 'Nalla Penn' (good girl) and 'Nalla Paiyan' (good boy).\nWhich statements are correct?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "1 and 2 only", "B": "2 and 3 only", "C": "1 and 3 only", "D": "All 1, 2, and 3 are correct"}, "explanation": "All three statements faithfully state the structural invariance of Dravidian adjectives documented by comparative linguists."}}, "question_data": {"assertion": null, "reason": null, "statements": [], "matching_pairs": [], "ordered_items": [], "numeric_answer": null, "passage_reference": null, "table_reference": null, "image_reference": null}, "answer": {"correct_key": "D", "accepted_keys": ["D"], "correct_order": [], "matching_answer": [], "numeric_value": null, "explanation_key": null}, "question_settings": {"is_negative_question": false, "marks": 1.5, "negative_marks": 0.0, "allow_multiple_answers": false}, "source": {"type": "book", "book_name": "Tamil Nadu Samacheer Kalvi", "publisher": "Tamil Nadu Textbook and Educational Services Corporation", "class": "9", "term": "full_year", "edition": "2024-2025", "page": 7, "chapter": null, "section": null, "reference": "9th Tamil, Unit 1, Page 7", "url": null, "source_notes": null}, "previous_year": {"is_previous_year": false, "exam": null, "exam_name": null, "year": null, "paper": null, "session": null}, "media": {"has_media": false, "items": []}, "tags": ["dravidian_adjectives", "caldwell_analysis", "statement_analysis"], "language_status": {"ta": "available", "en": "available"}, "workflow": {"status": "published", "verification_status": "verified", "created_by": "admin", "created_at": "2026-11-04T09:50:00Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-04T09:50:00Z"}, "version": {"current": 1, "previous_version_id": null, "revision_reason": null}}
{"id": "9th-u1-q033", "schema_version": "1.0", "kind": "assertion_reason", "level": "SSLC", "difficulty": "medium", "exam_mappings": ["group_4", "group_2", "group_2a"], "syllabus": {"class": "9", "subject_id": "general_tamil", "term": "full_year", "unit_id": "ta-9th-u1-mozhi", "lesson_id": "lesson-01-dravida-mozhi-kudumbam", "chapter_id": null, "topic_id": "topic-solvalam-semmozhi", "subtopic_id": null}, "texts": {"ta": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "கூற்று (A): ஒரே பொருளைக் குறிக்கப் பல சொற்கள் அமைந்த சொல்வளமும் சொல்லாட்சியும் நிரம்பிய பெருமொழி தமிழாகும்.\nகாரணம் (R): ஒரு தாவரத்தின் இலை நிலைகளை மட்டும் குறிக்க இலை, தாள், தோகை, ஓலை, சண்டு, சருகு எனப் பல நுட்பமான சொற்களைக் கொண்டுள்ள ஒரே மொழி தமிழ்.", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "கூற்று (A) மற்றும் காரணம் (R) இரண்டும் சரி; காரணம் கூற்றை விளக்குகிறது", "B": "கூற்று (A) சரி, ஆனால் காரணம் (R) தவறு", "C": "கூற்று (A) தவறு, ஆனால் காரணம் (R) சரி", "D": "கூற்று (A) மற்றும் காரணம் (R) இரண்டும் தவறு"}, "explanation": "தமிழின் நிகரற்ற சொல்வளத்திற்குத் தாவர உறுப்புகளின் பெயர்களே அசைக்க முடியாத சான்றாகும். கூற்று மற்றும் காரணம் இரண்டும் முற்றிலும் சரியானவை."}, "en": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "Assertion (A): Tamil is exceptionally renowned for its rich semantic vocabulary, using distinct words to describe micro-variations of a single entity.\nReason (R): For instance, Tamil possesses specialized vocabulary for different stages of plant leaves (Ilai, Thaal, Thogai, Olai, Sandu, Sarugu).", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "Both Assertion (A) and Reason (R) are correct, and (R) correctly explains (A)", "B": "(A) is correct, but (R) is false", "C": "(A) is false, but (R) is true", "D": "Both (A) and (R) are false"}, "explanation": "Both (A) and (R) are factually true and illustrate the exquisite botanical and lexical precision of Tamil."}}, "question_data": {"assertion": null, "reason": null, "statements": [], "matching_pairs": [], "ordered_items": [], "numeric_answer": null, "passage_reference": null, "table_reference": null, "image_reference": null}, "answer": {"correct_key": "A", "accepted_keys": ["A"], "correct_order": [], "matching_answer": [], "numeric_value": null, "explanation_key": null}, "question_settings": {"is_negative_question": false, "marks": 1.5, "negative_marks": 0.0, "allow_multiple_answers": false}, "source": {"type": "book", "book_name": "Tamil Nadu Samacheer Kalvi", "publisher": "Tamil Nadu Textbook and Educational Services Corporation", "class": "9", "term": "full_year", "edition": "2024-2025", "page": 9, "chapter": null, "section": null, "reference": "9th Tamil, Unit 1, Page 9", "url": null, "source_notes": null}, "previous_year": {"is_previous_year": false, "exam": null, "exam_name": null, "year": null, "paper": null, "session": null}, "media": {"has_media": false, "items": []}, "tags": ["tamil_richness", "vocabulary_precision", "assertion_reason"], "language_status": {"ta": "available", "en": "available"}, "workflow": {"status": "published", "verification_status": "verified", "created_by": "admin", "created_at": "2026-11-04T09:50:00Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-04T09:50:00Z"}, "version": {"current": 1, "previous_version_id": null, "revision_reason": null}}
{"id": "9th-u1-q034", "schema_version": "1.0", "kind": "statement_analysis", "level": "SSLC", "difficulty": "hard", "exam_mappings": ["group_4", "group_2", "group_2a"], "syllabus": {"class": "9", "subject_id": "general_tamil", "term": "full_year", "unit_id": "ta-9th-u1-mozhi", "lesson_id": "lesson-01-dravida-mozhi-kudumbam", "chapter_id": null, "topic_id": "topic-dravidian-linguistics-timeline", "subtopic_id": null}, "texts": {"ta": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "திராவிட மொழியியல் வரலாற்று மைல்கற்கள் குறித்த பின்வரும் கூற்றுகளைக் காலவரிசைப்படி ஆராய்க:\n1. 1786 - சர் வில்லியம் ஜோன்ஸ் வடமொழிக்கும் ஐரோப்பிய மொழிகளுக்கும் உள்ள உறவை அறிவித்தார்.\n2. 1816 - பிரான்சிஸ் எல்லிஸ் தென்னிந்திய மொழிகளைத் தனிக்குடும்பம் என நிறுவி 'தமிழிக்' என்றார்.\n3. 1856 - ராபர்ட் கால்டுவெல் 'திராவிட மொழிகளின் ஒப்பிலக்கணம்' நூலை வெளியிட்டார்.\nமேற்கண்ட கூற்றுகளுள் சரியான காலவரிசை அமைந்தவை எவை?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "1, 2 மட்டும் சரி", "B": "அனைத்தும் சரி", "C": "2, 3 மட்டும் சரி", "D": "1, 3 மட்டும் சரி"}, "explanation": "1786 (வில்லியம் ஜோன்ஸ்) → 1816 (பிரான்சிஸ் எல்லிஸ்) → 1856 (கால்டுவெல்) ஆகிய மூன்று வரலாற்று நிகழ்வுகளும் மிகத் துல்லியமான ஆண்டுகள். எனவே அனைத்தும் சரியானவை."}, "en": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "Examine the chronological milestones of Dravidian linguistic research:\n1. 1786 - Sir William Jones proposed Sanskrit's genealogical affinity with Indo-European languages.\n2. 1816 - F.W. Ellis classified South Indian languages as an autonomous family named 'Tamulic'.\n3. 1856 - Robert Caldwell published his magnum opus 'A Comparative Grammar of the Dravidian Languages'.\nWhich chronological milestones are correct?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "1 and 2 only are correct", "B": "All 1, 2, and 3 are correct", "C": "2 and 3 only are correct", "D": "1 and 3 only are correct"}, "explanation": "All three dates (1786, 1816, 1856) represent landmark historical moments in Indian comparative linguistics."}}, "question_data": {"assertion": null, "reason": null, "statements": [], "matching_pairs": [], "ordered_items": [], "numeric_answer": null, "passage_reference": null, "table_reference": null, "image_reference": null}, "answer": {"correct_key": "B", "accepted_keys": ["B"], "correct_order": [], "matching_answer": [], "numeric_value": null, "explanation_key": null}, "question_settings": {"is_negative_question": false, "marks": 1.5, "negative_marks": 0.0, "allow_multiple_answers": false}, "source": {"type": "book", "book_name": "Tamil Nadu Samacheer Kalvi", "publisher": "Tamil Nadu Textbook and Educational Services Corporation", "class": "9", "term": "full_year", "edition": "2024-2025", "page": 5, "chapter": null, "section": null, "reference": "9th Tamil, Unit 1, Page 5", "url": null, "source_notes": null}, "previous_year": {"is_previous_year": false, "exam": null, "exam_name": null, "year": null, "paper": null, "session": null}, "media": {"has_media": false, "items": []}, "tags": ["chronology", "linguistics_history", "statement_analysis"], "language_status": {"ta": "available", "en": "available"}, "workflow": {"status": "published", "verification_status": "verified", "created_by": "admin", "created_at": "2026-11-04T09:50:00Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-04T09:50:00Z"}, "version": {"current": 1, "previous_version_id": null, "revision_reason": null}}
{"id": "9th-u1-q035", "schema_version": "1.0", "kind": "matching", "level": "SSLC", "difficulty": "medium", "exam_mappings": ["group_4", "group_2", "group_2a"], "syllabus": {"class": "9", "subject_id": "general_tamil", "term": "full_year", "unit_id": "ta-9th-u1-mozhi", "lesson_id": "lesson-01-dravida-mozhi-kudumbam", "chapter_id": null, "topic_id": "topic-onru-irandu-matching", "subtopic_id": null}, "texts": {"ta": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "'ஒன்று' மற்றும் 'ஐந்து' ஆகிய தமிழெண்களின் திராவிட மொழி வடிவங்களைப் பொருத்துக:\nபட்டியல் I:\na) ஒன்று (மலையாளம்)\nb) ஒன்று (தெலுங்கு)\nc) ஐந்து (மலையாளம்)\nd) ஐந்து (கன்னடம்)\n\nபட்டியல் II:\n1. ஒக்கட்டி\n2. ஐது\n3. அஞ்சு\n4. ஒன்னு", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "a-1, b-4, c-2, d-3", "B": "a-4, b-1, c-2, d-3", "C": "a-4, b-1, c-3, d-2", "D": "a-3, b-2, c-4, d-1"}, "explanation": "ஒன்று: மலையாளம் = ஒன்னு (4); தெலுங்கு = ஒக்கட்டி (1). ஐந்து: மலையாளம் = அஞ்சு (3); கன்னடம் = ஐது (2). சரியான பொருத்தம்: 4, 1, 3, 2."}, "en": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "Match the Tamil numerals 'One' and 'Five' with their cognate forms in sister languages:\nList I: a) One (Malayalam), b) One (Telugu), c) Five (Malayalam), d) Five (Kannada)\nList II: 1. Okkati, 2. Aidu, 3. Anchu, 4. Onnu", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "a-1, b-4, c-2, d-3", "B": "a-4, b-1, c-2, d-3", "C": "a-4, b-1, c-3, d-2", "D": "a-3, b-2, c-4, d-1"}, "explanation": "One: Malayalam = Onnu (4); Telugu = Okkati (1). Five: Malayalam = Anchu (3); Kannada = Aidu (2). Order: 4, 1, 3, 2."}}, "question_data": {"assertion": null, "reason": null, "statements": [], "matching_pairs": [], "ordered_items": [], "numeric_answer": null, "passage_reference": null, "table_reference": null, "image_reference": null}, "answer": {"correct_key": "C", "accepted_keys": ["C"], "correct_order": [], "matching_answer": [], "numeric_value": null, "explanation_key": null}, "question_settings": {"is_negative_question": false, "marks": 1.5, "negative_marks": 0.0, "allow_multiple_answers": false}, "source": {"type": "book", "book_name": "Tamil Nadu Samacheer Kalvi", "publisher": "Tamil Nadu Textbook and Educational Services Corporation", "class": "9", "term": "full_year", "edition": "2024-2025", "page": 7, "chapter": null, "section": null, "reference": "9th Tamil, Unit 1, Page 7", "url": null, "source_notes": null}, "previous_year": {"is_previous_year": false, "exam": null, "exam_name": null, "year": null, "paper": null, "session": null}, "media": {"has_media": false, "items": []}, "tags": ["numerals", "dravidian_cognates", "matching"], "language_status": {"ta": "available", "en": "available"}, "workflow": {"status": "published", "verification_status": "verified", "created_by": "admin", "created_at": "2026-11-04T09:50:00Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-04T09:50:00Z"}, "version": {"current": 1, "previous_version_id": null, "revision_reason": null}}
{"id": "9th-u1-q036", "schema_version": "1.0", "kind": "direct", "level": "SSLC", "difficulty": "medium", "exam_mappings": ["group_4", "group_2", "group_2a"], "syllabus": {"class": "9", "subject_id": "general_tamil", "term": "full_year", "unit_id": "ta-9th-u1-mozhi", "lesson_id": "lesson-01-dravida-mozhi-kudumbam", "chapter_id": null, "topic_id": "topic-mooladravida-kootru", "subtopic_id": null}, "texts": {"ta": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "திராவிட மொழிகளுள் மூலத் திராவிட மொழியின் (Proto-Dravidian) பண்புகள் பலவற்றையும் சிதையாமல் அப்படியே பாதுகாத்து வரும் முதன்மை மொழி எது?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "கன்னடம்", "B": "தெலுங்கு", "C": "மலையாளம்", "D": "தமிழ்"}, "explanation": "பாடநூல் பக். 9-இன் படி: 'மூலத் திராவிட மொழியின் பண்புகள் பலவற்றையும் பேணிப் பாதுகாத்து வரும் தன்மையே தமிழின் தனித்தன்மையாக விளங்குகிறது'."}, "en": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "Which Dravidian language has preserved the structural and grammatical traits of Proto-Dravidian with the greatest fidelity?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "Kannada", "B": "Telugu", "C": "Malayalam", "D": "Tamil"}, "explanation": "Tamil preserves the characteristics of the Proto-Dravidian parent language far more intact than any other descendant language."}}, "question_data": {"assertion": null, "reason": null, "statements": [], "matching_pairs": [], "ordered_items": [], "numeric_answer": null, "passage_reference": null, "table_reference": null, "image_reference": null}, "answer": {"correct_key": "D", "accepted_keys": ["D"], "correct_order": [], "matching_answer": [], "numeric_value": null, "explanation_key": null}, "question_settings": {"is_negative_question": false, "marks": 1.5, "negative_marks": 0.0, "allow_multiple_answers": false}, "source": {"type": "book", "book_name": "Tamil Nadu Samacheer Kalvi", "publisher": "Tamil Nadu Textbook and Educational Services Corporation", "class": "9", "term": "full_year", "edition": "2024-2025", "page": 9, "chapter": null, "section": null, "reference": "9th Tamil, Unit 1, Page 9", "url": null, "source_notes": null}, "previous_year": {"is_previous_year": false, "exam": null, "exam_name": null, "year": null, "paper": null, "session": null}, "media": {"has_media": false, "items": []}, "tags": ["proto_dravidian", "tamil_purity", "direct_mcq"], "language_status": {"ta": "available", "en": "available"}, "workflow": {"status": "published", "verification_status": "verified", "created_by": "admin", "created_at": "2026-11-04T09:50:00Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-04T09:50:00Z"}, "version": {"current": 1, "previous_version_id": null, "revision_reason": null}}
{"id": "9th-u1-q037", "schema_version": "1.0", "kind": "statement_analysis", "level": "SSLC", "difficulty": "medium", "exam_mappings": ["group_4", "group_2", "group_2a"], "syllabus": {"class": "9", "subject_id": "general_tamil", "term": "full_year", "unit_id": "ta-9th-u1-mozhi", "lesson_id": "lesson-01-dravida-mozhi-kudumbam", "chapter_id": null, "topic_id": "topic-telugu-antiquity", "subtopic_id": null}, "texts": {"ta": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "தெலுங்கு மொழியின் தொன்மை சான்றுகள் குறித்த பின்வரும் கூற்றுகளை ஆராய்க:\n1. தெலுங்கின் மிகத் தொன்மையான இலக்கிய நூல் 'பாரதம்' நன்னையாவால் 11-ஆம் நூற்றாண்டில் இயற்றப்பட்டது.\n2. தெலுங்கின் மிகத் தொன்மையான இலக்கண நூல் 'ஆந்திர பாஷா பூஷணம்' 12-ஆம் நூற்றாண்டைச் சேர்ந்தது.\n3. தெலுங்குக் கல்வெட்டுச் சான்றுகள் கி.பி. 6-ஆம் நூற்றாண்டைச் சேர்ந்த கலமல்லா கல்வெட்டு முதல் கிடைக்கின்றன.\nமேற்கண்ட கூற்றுகளுள் சரியானவை எவை?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "அனைத்தும் சரி", "B": "1, 2 மட்டும் சரி", "C": "2, 3 மட்டும் சரி", "D": "1, 3 மட்டும் சரி"}, "explanation": "பாடநூல் பக். 8 அட்டவணையின்படி: தெலுங்கு இலக்கியம் பாரதம் (கி.பி. 11), இலக்கணம் ஆந்திர பாஷா பூஷணம் (கி.பி. 12), கல்வெட்டுகள் கி.பி. 6-ஆம் நூற்றாண்டு முதல் கிடைக்கின்றன. அனைத்தும் சரியானவை."}, "en": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "Examine the statements regarding the antiquity of Telugu:\n1. The earliest Telugu literary work is the Mahabharata adapted by Nannaya in the 11th century CE.\n2. The earliest extant Telugu grammar is Andhra Bhasha Bhushanam from the 12th century CE.\n3. Telugu epigraphical rock inscriptions are attested from the 6th century CE onwards (e.g. Kalamalla inscription).\nWhich statements are correct?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "All are correct", "B": "1 and 2 only are correct", "C": "2 and 3 only are correct", "D": "1 and 3 only are correct"}, "explanation": "All three facts align precisely with textbook page 8 comparative data."}}, "question_data": {"assertion": null, "reason": null, "statements": [], "matching_pairs": [], "ordered_items": [], "numeric_answer": null, "passage_reference": null, "table_reference": null, "image_reference": null}, "answer": {"correct_key": "A", "accepted_keys": ["A"], "correct_order": [], "matching_answer": [], "numeric_value": null, "explanation_key": null}, "question_settings": {"is_negative_question": false, "marks": 1.5, "negative_marks": 0.0, "allow_multiple_answers": false}, "source": {"type": "book", "book_name": "Tamil Nadu Samacheer Kalvi", "publisher": "Tamil Nadu Textbook and Educational Services Corporation", "class": "9", "term": "full_year", "edition": "2024-2025", "page": 8, "chapter": null, "section": null, "reference": "9th Tamil, Unit 1, Page 8", "url": null, "source_notes": null}, "previous_year": {"is_previous_year": false, "exam": null, "exam_name": null, "year": null, "paper": null, "session": null}, "media": {"has_media": false, "items": []}, "tags": ["telugu_antiquity", "table_data", "statement_analysis"], "language_status": {"ta": "available", "en": "available"}, "workflow": {"status": "published", "verification_status": "verified", "created_by": "admin", "created_at": "2026-11-04T09:50:00Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-04T09:50:00Z"}, "version": {"current": 1, "previous_version_id": null, "revision_reason": null}}
{"id": "9th-u1-q038", "schema_version": "1.0", "kind": "odd_one_out", "level": "SSLC", "difficulty": "medium", "exam_mappings": ["group_4", "group_2", "group_2a"], "syllabus": {"class": "9", "subject_id": "general_tamil", "term": "full_year", "unit_id": "ta-9th-u1-mozhi", "lesson_id": "lesson-01-dravida-mozhi-kudumbam", "chapter_id": null, "topic_id": "topic-neelagiri-tribal-tongues", "subtopic_id": null}, "texts": {"ta": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "நீலகிரி மற்றும் அதை ஒட்டிய தென்னக மலைப்பகுதிகளில் பேசப்படும் திராவிடப் பழங்குடி மொழிகளுள் சேராத ஒன்றைக் கண்டறிக:", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "தோடா", "B": "பிராகுய்", "C": "கோத்தா", "D": "இருளா"}, "explanation": "தோடா, கோத்தா, இருளா ஆகியவை நீலகிரி மலைகளில் பேசப்படும் தென் திராவிட மொழிகள். பிராகுய் என்பது பாகிஸ்தானின் பலுசிஸ்தானில் பேசப்படும் வட திராவிட மொழி."}, "en": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "Identify the language that is NOT a South Dravidian tribal tongue native to the Nilgiri mountainous tracts:", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "Toda", "B": "Brahui", "C": "Kota", "D": "Irula"}, "explanation": "Brahui is spoken thousands of kilometers away in Balochistan (Pakistan), unlike Toda, Kota, and Irula of the Nilgiris."}}, "question_data": {"assertion": null, "reason": null, "statements": [], "matching_pairs": [], "ordered_items": [], "numeric_answer": null, "passage_reference": null, "table_reference": null, "image_reference": null}, "answer": {"correct_key": "B", "accepted_keys": ["B"], "correct_order": [], "matching_answer": [], "numeric_value": null, "explanation_key": null}, "question_settings": {"is_negative_question": false, "marks": 1.5, "negative_marks": 0.0, "allow_multiple_answers": false}, "source": {"type": "book", "book_name": "Tamil Nadu Samacheer Kalvi", "publisher": "Tamil Nadu Textbook and Educational Services Corporation", "class": "9", "term": "full_year", "edition": "2024-2025", "page": 6, "chapter": null, "section": null, "reference": "9th Tamil, Unit 1, Page 6", "url": null, "source_notes": null}, "previous_year": {"is_previous_year": false, "exam": null, "exam_name": null, "year": null, "paper": null, "session": null}, "media": {"has_media": false, "items": []}, "tags": ["tribal_languages", "nilgiris", "odd_one_out"], "language_status": {"ta": "available", "en": "available"}, "workflow": {"status": "published", "verification_status": "verified", "created_by": "admin", "created_at": "2026-11-04T09:50:00Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-04T09:50:00Z"}, "version": {"current": 1, "previous_version_id": null, "revision_reason": null}}
{"id": "9th-u1-q039", "schema_version": "1.0", "kind": "direct", "level": "SSLC", "difficulty": "medium", "exam_mappings": ["group_4", "group_2", "group_2a"], "syllabus": {"class": "9", "subject_id": "general_tamil", "term": "full_year", "unit_id": "ta-9th-u1-mozhi", "lesson_id": "lesson-01-dravida-mozhi-kudumbam", "chapter_id": null, "topic_id": "topic-tholkappiyam-date", "subtopic_id": null}, "texts": {"ta": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "திராவிட மொழிகளிலேயே மிகத் தொன்மையான இலக்கண நூலான 'தொல்காப்பியம்' எந்தக் காலத்தைச் சேர்ந்ததாகப் பாடநூல் அட்டவணையில் குறிப்பிடப்பட்டுள்ளது?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "கி.பி. 1-ஆம் நூற்றாண்டு", "B": "கி.பி. 3-ஆம் நூற்றாண்டு", "C": "கி.மு. 3-ஆம் நூற்றாண்டு அளவில்", "D": "கி.மு. 5-ஆம் நூற்றாண்டு"}, "explanation": "பாடநூல் பக். 8 அட்டவணையில்: தமிழ் இலக்கணம் தொல்காப்பியத்தின் காலம் 'கி.மு. 3-ஆம் நூற்றாண்டு அளவில்' எனக் குறிக்கப்பட்டுள்ளது."}, "en": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "In the comparative antiquity chart, to which approximate period is Tholkappiyam dated?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "1st Century CE", "B": "3rd Century CE", "C": "Circa 3rd Century BCE", "D": "5th Century BCE"}, "explanation": "Textbook page 8 lists Tholkappiyam's antiquity as approximately 3rd Century BCE."}}, "question_data": {"assertion": null, "reason": null, "statements": [], "matching_pairs": [], "ordered_items": [], "numeric_answer": null, "passage_reference": null, "table_reference": null, "image_reference": null}, "answer": {"correct_key": "C", "accepted_keys": ["C"], "correct_order": [], "matching_answer": [], "numeric_value": null, "explanation_key": null}, "question_settings": {"is_negative_question": false, "marks": 1.5, "negative_marks": 0.0, "allow_multiple_answers": false}, "source": {"type": "book", "book_name": "Tamil Nadu Samacheer Kalvi", "publisher": "Tamil Nadu Textbook and Educational Services Corporation", "class": "9", "term": "full_year", "edition": "2024-2025", "page": 8, "chapter": null, "section": null, "reference": "9th Tamil, Unit 1, Page 8", "url": null, "source_notes": null}, "previous_year": {"is_previous_year": false, "exam": null, "exam_name": null, "year": null, "paper": null, "session": null}, "media": {"has_media": false, "items": []}, "tags": ["tholkappiyam", "antiquity_date", "direct_mcq"], "language_status": {"ta": "available", "en": "available"}, "workflow": {"status": "published", "verification_status": "verified", "created_by": "admin", "created_at": "2026-11-04T09:50:00Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-04T09:50:00Z"}, "version": {"current": 1, "previous_version_id": null, "revision_reason": null}}
{"id": "9th-u1-q040", "schema_version": "1.0", "kind": "statement_analysis", "level": "SSLC", "difficulty": "hard", "exam_mappings": ["group_4", "group_2", "group_2a"], "syllabus": {"class": "9", "subject_id": "general_tamil", "term": "full_year", "unit_id": "ta-9th-u1-mozhi", "lesson_id": "lesson-01-dravida-mozhi-kudumbam", "chapter_id": null, "topic_id": "topic-malayalam-verb-exception", "subtopic_id": null}, "texts": {"ta": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "மலையாள மொழியின் இலக்கண அமைப்பு குறித்த பின்வரும் கூற்றுகளை ஆராய்க:\n1. மலையாளம் தமிழிலிருந்து கி.பி. 9 முதல் 12-ஆம் நூற்றாண்டுகளுக்கு இடைப்பட்ட காலத்தில் பிரிந்து தனிமொழியாக வளர்ந்தது.\n2. தமிழிலும் கன்னடத்திலும் வினைகள் பால் காட்டும் விகுதிகளைப் பெற்றிருக்கும் போது, மலையாளத்தில் அவை மறைந்து போயின.\n3. 'அவன் வந்தான்', 'அவள் வந்தாள்' என்பதற்குப் பதிலாக மலையாளத்தில் 'அவன் வந்நு', 'அவள் வந்நு' என்றே வரும்.\nமேற்கண்டவற்றுள் சரியான கூற்றுகள் எவை?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "1, 2 மட்டும்", "B": "2, 3 மட்டும்", "C": "1, 3 மட்டும்", "D": "அனைத்தும் சரி"}, "explanation": "மூன்று கூற்றுகளும் மலையாள மொழியின் வரலாற்று வளர்ச்சி மற்றும் அதன் தனித்துவமான பால் காட்டா வினைமுற்று அமைப்பை மிகச் சரியாக விளக்குகின்றன."}, "en": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "Examine the statements regarding Malayalam grammatical structure:\n1. Malayalam branched off from Old Tamil between the 9th and 12th centuries CE.\n2. While Tamil and Kannada preserve verbal gender inflections, Malayalam shed these suffixes over time.\n3. Instead of gender-marked verbs ('Vandhaan'/'Vandhaal'), Malayalam uniformly uses gender-neutral forms ('Vannu').\nWhich statements are correct?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "1 and 2 only", "B": "2 and 3 only", "C": "1 and 3 only", "D": "All 1, 2, and 3 are correct"}, "explanation": "All three statements accurately reflect the comparative linguistic evolution of Malayalam from the parent Tamil stock."}}, "question_data": {"assertion": null, "reason": null, "statements": [], "matching_pairs": [], "ordered_items": [], "numeric_answer": null, "passage_reference": null, "table_reference": null, "image_reference": null}, "answer": {"correct_key": "D", "accepted_keys": ["D"], "correct_order": [], "matching_answer": [], "numeric_value": null, "explanation_key": null}, "question_settings": {"is_negative_question": false, "marks": 1.5, "negative_marks": 0.0, "allow_multiple_answers": false}, "source": {"type": "book", "book_name": "Tamil Nadu Samacheer Kalvi", "publisher": "Tamil Nadu Textbook and Educational Services Corporation", "class": "9", "term": "full_year", "edition": "2024-2025", "page": 7, "chapter": null, "section": null, "reference": "9th Tamil, Unit 1, Page 7", "url": null, "source_notes": null}, "previous_year": {"is_previous_year": false, "exam": null, "exam_name": null, "year": null, "paper": null, "session": null}, "media": {"has_media": false, "items": []}, "tags": ["malayalam", "linguistic_evolution", "statement_analysis"], "language_status": {"ta": "available", "en": "available"}, "workflow": {"status": "published", "verification_status": "verified", "created_by": "admin", "created_at": "2026-11-04T09:50:00Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-04T09:50:00Z"}, "version": {"current": 1, "previous_version_id": null, "revision_reason": null}}
{"id": "9th-u1-q041", "schema_version": "1.0", "kind": "matching", "level": "SSLC", "difficulty": "medium", "exam_mappings": ["group_4", "group_2", "group_2a"], "syllabus": {"class": "9", "subject_id": "general_tamil", "term": "full_year", "unit_id": "ta-9th-u1-mozhi", "lesson_id": "lesson-01-dravida-mozhi-kudumbam", "chapter_id": null, "topic_id": "topic-sister-tongues-literature", "subtopic_id": null}, "texts": {"ta": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "திராவிட மொழிகளின் இலக்கியங்களையும் அவற்றுக்குரிய மொழிகளையும் பொருத்துக:\nபட்டியல் I:\na) சங்க இலக்கியம்\nb) கவிராஜமார்க்கம்\nc) பாரதம் (நன்னையா)\nd) ராமசரிதம்\n\nபட்டியல் II:\n1. தெலுங்கு\n2. மலையாளம்\n3. கன்னடம்\n4. தமிழ்", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "a-4, b-3, c-1, d-2", "B": "a-4, b-1, c-3, d-2", "C": "a-3, b-4, c-1, d-2", "D": "a-2, b-3, c-1, d-4"}, "explanation": "சங்க இலக்கியம் = தமிழ் (4); கவிராஜமார்க்கம் = கன்னடம் (3); பாரதம் = தெலுங்கு (1); ராமசரிதம் = மலையாளம் (2). சரியான வரிசை: 4, 3, 1, 2."}, "en": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "Match the classical literary texts with their respective Dravidian languages:\nList I: a) Sangam Literature, b) Kavirajamarga, c) Bharatham, d) Ramacharitam\nList II: 1. Telugu, 2. Malayalam, 3. Kannada, 4. Tamil", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "a-4, b-3, c-1, d-2", "B": "a-4, b-1, c-3, d-2", "C": "a-3, b-4, c-1, d-2", "D": "a-2, b-3, c-1, d-4"}, "explanation": "Sangam: Tamil (4); Kavirajamarga: Kannada (3); Bharatham: Telugu (1); Ramacharitam: Malayalam (2). Order: 4, 3, 1, 2."}}, "question_data": {"assertion": null, "reason": null, "statements": [], "matching_pairs": [], "ordered_items": [], "numeric_answer": null, "passage_reference": null, "table_reference": null, "image_reference": null}, "answer": {"correct_key": "A", "accepted_keys": ["A"], "correct_order": [], "matching_answer": [], "numeric_value": null, "explanation_key": null}, "question_settings": {"is_negative_question": false, "marks": 1.5, "negative_marks": 0.0, "allow_multiple_answers": false}, "source": {"type": "book", "book_name": "Tamil Nadu Samacheer Kalvi", "publisher": "Tamil Nadu Textbook and Educational Services Corporation", "class": "9", "term": "full_year", "edition": "2024-2025", "page": 8, "chapter": null, "section": null, "reference": "9th Tamil, Unit 1, Page 8", "url": null, "source_notes": null}, "previous_year": {"is_previous_year": false, "exam": null, "exam_name": null, "year": null, "paper": null, "session": null}, "media": {"has_media": false, "items": []}, "tags": ["classical_texts", "matching", "comparative_antiquity"], "language_status": {"ta": "available", "en": "available"}, "workflow": {"status": "published", "verification_status": "verified", "created_by": "admin", "created_at": "2026-11-04T09:50:00Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-04T09:50:00Z"}, "version": {"current": 1, "previous_version_id": null, "revision_reason": null}}
{"id": "9th-u1-q042", "schema_version": "1.0", "kind": "assertion_reason", "level": "SSLC", "difficulty": "medium", "exam_mappings": ["group_4", "group_2", "group_2a"], "syllabus": {"class": "9", "subject_id": "general_tamil", "term": "full_year", "unit_id": "ta-9th-u1-mozhi", "lesson_id": "lesson-01-dravida-mozhi-kudumbam", "chapter_id": null, "topic_id": "topic-tamilin-thanithiyangum-aattral", "subtopic_id": null}, "texts": {"ta": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "கூற்று (A): தமிழ் மொழி பிற திராவிட மொழிகளுள் எதன் உதவியுமின்றித் தனித்து இயங்கும் ஆற்றல் பெற்றுள்ளது.\nகாரணம் (R): ஒரு மொழியின் வேர்ச்சொற்கள், இலக்கண விதிகள், தொடரமைப்பு ஆகிய மூன்றும் பிறமொழிகளைச் சாராமல் இருத்தலே அதன் தனித்தியங்கும் ஆற்றலுக்குச் சான்றாகும்.", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "கூற்று (A) சரி, ஆனால் காரணம் (R) தவறு", "B": "கூற்று (A) மற்றும் காரணம் (R) இரண்டும் சரி; காரணம் கூற்றை விளக்குகிறது", "C": "கூற்று (A) தவறு, ஆனால் காரணம் (R) சரி", "D": "கூற்று (A) மற்றும் காரணம் (R) இரண்டும் தவறு"}, "explanation": "தமிழ் தனித்தியங்கும் பேராற்றல் கொண்ட உயர்தனிச் செம்மொழி. அதன் வேர்ச்சொல் வளமும் இலக்கணக் கட்டமைப்பும் தன்னிறைவு பெற்றவை. கூற்று மற்றும் காரணம் இரண்டும் முற்றிலும் சரியானவை."}, "en": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "Assertion (A): Tamil possesses the vital capability to function completely autonomously without depending on any other language.\nReason (R): The autonomy of a language is evidenced when its root words, grammatical principles, and syntax operate self-sufficiently without foreign reliance.", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "(A) is true, but (R) is false", "B": "Both (A) and (R) are true, and (R) correctly explains (A)", "C": "(A) is false, but (R) is true", "D": "Both (A) and (R) are false"}, "explanation": "Tamil's self-contained lexical and morphological system gives it unmatched linguistic autonomy. Both statements are true."}}, "question_data": {"assertion": null, "reason": null, "statements": [], "matching_pairs": [], "ordered_items": [], "numeric_answer": null, "passage_reference": null, "table_reference": null, "image_reference": null}, "answer": {"correct_key": "B", "accepted_keys": ["B"], "correct_order": [], "matching_answer": [], "numeric_value": null, "explanation_key": null}, "question_settings": {"is_negative_question": false, "marks": 1.5, "negative_marks": 0.0, "allow_multiple_answers": false}, "source": {"type": "book", "book_name": "Tamil Nadu Samacheer Kalvi", "publisher": "Tamil Nadu Textbook and Educational Services Corporation", "class": "9", "term": "full_year", "edition": "2024-2025", "page": 9, "chapter": null, "section": null, "reference": "9th Tamil, Unit 1, Page 9", "url": null, "source_notes": null}, "previous_year": {"is_previous_year": false, "exam": null, "exam_name": null, "year": null, "paper": null, "session": null}, "media": {"has_media": false, "items": []}, "tags": ["tamil_autonomy", "linguistics", "assertion_reason"], "language_status": {"ta": "available", "en": "available"}, "workflow": {"status": "published", "verification_status": "verified", "created_by": "admin", "created_at": "2026-11-04T09:50:00Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-04T09:50:00Z"}, "version": {"current": 1, "previous_version_id": null, "revision_reason": null}}
{"id": "9th-u1-q043", "schema_version": "1.0", "kind": "direct", "level": "SSLC", "difficulty": "easy", "exam_mappings": ["group_4", "group_2", "group_2a"], "syllabus": {"class": "9", "subject_id": "general_tamil", "term": "full_year", "unit_id": "ta-9th-u1-mozhi", "lesson_id": "lesson-01-dravida-mozhi-kudumbam", "chapter_id": null, "topic_id": "topic-recently-identified-languages", "subtopic_id": null}, "texts": {"ta": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "திராவிட மொழிகள் பட்டியலில் அண்மையில் சேர்க்கப்பட்ட நான்கு மொழிகள் எவை?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "குரூக், மால்தோ, பிராகுய், தோடா", "B": "கூயி, கூவி, கோண்டா, கோலாமி", "C": "எருகலா, தங்கா, குறும்பா, சோளிகா", "D": "பர்ஜி, கதபா, பெங்கோ, மண்டா"}, "explanation": "பாடநூல் பக். 6-இல் உள்ள குறிப்பு: 'அண்மையில் கண்டறியப்பட்ட எருகலா, தங்கா, குறும்பா, சோளிகா ஆகிய நான்கு மொழிகளையும் சேர்த்துத் திராவிட மொழிகள் மொத்தம் 28 ஆகும்'."}, "en": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "Which four languages were recently recognized and added to the official count of Dravidian languages?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "Kurukh, Malto, Brahui, and Toda", "B": "Kui, Kuvi, Konda, and Kolami", "C": "Erukala, Thanga, Kurumba, and Soliga", "D": "Parji, Gadaba, Pengo, and Manda"}, "explanation": "The 4 recently cataloged additions specified on page 6 are Erukala, Thanga, Kurumba, and Soliga."}}, "question_data": {"assertion": null, "reason": null, "statements": [], "matching_pairs": [], "ordered_items": [], "numeric_answer": null, "passage_reference": null, "table_reference": null, "image_reference": null}, "answer": {"correct_key": "C", "accepted_keys": ["C"], "correct_order": [], "matching_answer": [], "numeric_value": null, "explanation_key": null}, "question_settings": {"is_negative_question": false, "marks": 1.5, "negative_marks": 0.0, "allow_multiple_answers": false}, "source": {"type": "book", "book_name": "Tamil Nadu Samacheer Kalvi", "publisher": "Tamil Nadu Textbook and Educational Services Corporation", "class": "9", "term": "full_year", "edition": "2024-2025", "page": 6, "chapter": null, "section": null, "reference": "9th Tamil, Unit 1, Page 6", "url": null, "source_notes": null}, "previous_year": {"is_previous_year": false, "exam": null, "exam_name": null, "year": null, "paper": null, "session": null}, "media": {"has_media": false, "items": []}, "tags": ["dravidian_recent_additions", "direct_mcq"], "language_status": {"ta": "available", "en": "available"}, "workflow": {"status": "published", "verification_status": "verified", "created_by": "admin", "created_at": "2026-11-04T09:50:00Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-04T09:50:00Z"}, "version": {"current": 1, "previous_version_id": null, "revision_reason": null}}
{"id": "9th-u1-q044", "schema_version": "1.0", "kind": "statement_analysis", "level": "SSLC", "difficulty": "medium", "exam_mappings": ["group_4", "group_2", "group_2a"], "syllabus": {"class": "9", "subject_id": "general_tamil", "term": "full_year", "unit_id": "ta-9th-u1-mozhi", "lesson_id": "lesson-01-dravida-mozhi-kudumbam", "chapter_id": null, "topic_id": "topic-tulu-characteristics", "subtopic_id": null}, "texts": {"ta": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "துளு மொழி குறித்த பின்வரும் கூற்றுகளை ஆராய்க:\n1. துளு தென் திராவிட மொழிக் குடும்பத்தைச் சேர்ந்த ஒரு மொழியாகும்.\n2. கர்நாடகத்தின் கடற்கரை மாவட்டங்களான தட்சிண கன்னடா மற்றும் உடுப்பி பகுதிகளில் துளு பேசப்படுகிறது.\n3. துளு மொழியில் எண்ணுப்பெயர் 'மூன்று' என்பது 'மூஜி' என வழங்குகிறது.\nமேற்கண்ட கூற்றுகளுள் சரியானவை எவை?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "1, 2 மட்டும்", "B": "2, 3 மட்டும்", "C": "1, 3 மட்டும்", "D": "அனைத்தும் சரி"}, "explanation": "துளு தென் திராவிட மொழி; கடலோர கர்நாடகத்தில் பேசப்படுகிறது; 'மூன்று' என்பது 'மூஜி' எனவும் 'நான்கு' என்பது 'நாலு' எனவும் துளுவில் வழங்குகிறது. அனைத்துக் கூற்றுகளும் சரியானவை."}, "en": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "Examine the statements concerning the Tulu language:\n1. Tulu is classified under the South Dravidian sub-family.\n2. It is predominantly spoken in coastal Karnataka districts like Dakshina Kannada and Udupi.\n3. The numeral 'Three' is pronounced as 'Mooji' in Tulu.\nWhich statements are correct?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "1 and 2 only", "B": "2 and 3 only", "C": "1 and 3 only", "D": "All 1, 2, and 3 are correct"}, "explanation": "All three statements faithfully state the geographic and morphological traits of Tulu."}}, "question_data": {"assertion": null, "reason": null, "statements": [], "matching_pairs": [], "ordered_items": [], "numeric_answer": null, "passage_reference": null, "table_reference": null, "image_reference": null}, "answer": {"correct_key": "D", "accepted_keys": ["D"], "correct_order": [], "matching_answer": [], "numeric_value": null, "explanation_key": null}, "question_settings": {"is_negative_question": false, "marks": 1.5, "negative_marks": 0.0, "allow_multiple_answers": false}, "source": {"type": "book", "book_name": "Tamil Nadu Samacheer Kalvi", "publisher": "Tamil Nadu Textbook and Educational Services Corporation", "class": "9", "term": "full_year", "edition": "2024-2025", "page": 6, "chapter": null, "section": null, "reference": "9th Tamil, Unit 1, Page 6", "url": null, "source_notes": null}, "previous_year": {"is_previous_year": false, "exam": null, "exam_name": null, "year": null, "paper": null, "session": null}, "media": {"has_media": false, "items": []}, "tags": ["tulu", "south_dravidian", "statement_analysis"], "language_status": {"ta": "available", "en": "available"}, "workflow": {"status": "published", "verification_status": "verified", "created_by": "admin", "created_at": "2026-11-04T09:50:00Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-04T09:50:00Z"}, "version": {"current": 1, "previous_version_id": null, "revision_reason": null}}
{"id": "9th-u1-q045", "schema_version": "1.0", "kind": "direct", "level": "SSLC", "difficulty": "medium", "exam_mappings": ["group_4", "group_2", "group_2a"], "syllabus": {"class": "9", "subject_id": "general_tamil", "term": "full_year", "unit_id": "ta-9th-u1-mozhi", "lesson_id": "lesson-01-dravida-mozhi-kudumbam", "chapter_id": null, "topic_id": "topic-dravida-sol-thotram", "subtopic_id": null}, "texts": {"ta": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "'தமிழ்' என்னும் சொல்லிலிருந்தே 'திராவிடம்' என்னும் சொல் பிறந்தது என்று மொழியியல் அடிப்படையில் விளக்கிய பாதிரியார் யார்?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "ஹீராஸ் பாதிரியார்", "B": "கால்டுவெல் பாதிரியார்", "C": "போப் பாதிரியார்", "D": "பெஸ்கி பாதிரியார்"}, "explanation": "ஹீராஸ் பாதிரியார் தமிழ் என்னும் சொல்லிலிருந்து 'திராவிடம்' உருவான ஒலி மாற்றத்தை (தமிழ் → தமழா → த்ரமில → த்ரமிட → த்ராவிட → திராவிடம்) விளக்கினார்."}, "en": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "Which historian-priest demonstrated phonologically that the word 'Dravida' was derived directly from the word 'Tamil'?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "Father Heras", "B": "Bishop Caldwell", "C": "Rev. G.U. Pope", "D": "Father Beschi"}, "explanation": "Father Henry Heras demonstrated the historical linguistic trajectory leading from 'Tamil' to 'Dravidam'."}}, "question_data": {"assertion": null, "reason": null, "statements": [], "matching_pairs": [], "ordered_items": [], "numeric_answer": null, "passage_reference": null, "table_reference": null, "image_reference": null}, "answer": {"correct_key": "A", "accepted_keys": ["A"], "correct_order": [], "matching_answer": [], "numeric_value": null, "explanation_key": null}, "question_settings": {"is_negative_question": false, "marks": 1.5, "negative_marks": 0.0, "allow_multiple_answers": false}, "source": {"type": "book", "book_name": "Tamil Nadu Samacheer Kalvi", "publisher": "Tamil Nadu Textbook and Educational Services Corporation", "class": "9", "term": "full_year", "edition": "2024-2025", "page": 5, "chapter": null, "section": null, "reference": "9th Tamil, Unit 1, Page 5", "url": null, "source_notes": null}, "previous_year": {"is_previous_year": false, "exam": null, "exam_name": null, "year": null, "paper": null, "session": null}, "media": {"has_media": false, "items": []}, "tags": ["heras", "etymology", "direct_mcq"], "language_status": {"ta": "available", "en": "available"}, "workflow": {"status": "published", "verification_status": "verified", "created_by": "admin", "created_at": "2026-11-04T09:50:00Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-04T09:50:00Z"}, "version": {"current": 1, "previous_version_id": null, "revision_reason": null}}
{"id": "9th-u1-q046", "schema_version": "1.0", "kind": "statement_analysis", "level": "SSLC", "difficulty": "hard", "exam_mappings": ["group_4", "group_2", "group_2a"], "syllabus": {"class": "9", "subject_id": "general_tamil", "term": "full_year", "unit_id": "ta-9th-u1-mozhi", "lesson_id": "lesson-01-dravida-mozhi-kudumbam", "chapter_id": null, "topic_id": "topic-dravida-podhukkoorugal", "subtopic_id": null}, "texts": {"ta": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "திராவிட மொழிகளின் பொதுக்கூறுகள் குறித்த பின்வரும் கூற்றுகளை ஆராய்க:\n1. திராவிட மொழிகளில் பெரும்பாலானவை ஒட்டுநிலை (Agglutinative) மொழிகளாக விளங்குகின்றன.\n2. சொற்களின் வேர்ச்சொல்லோடு விகுதிகள் ஒன்றன் பின் ஒன்றாக இணைந்து புதிய பொருளைத் தருகின்றன.\n3. வடமொழியைப் போலன்றித் திராவிட மொழிகளில் சொற்களின் வேர் வடிவம் பெரும்பாலும் மாறாமல் மூலப் பொருளைக் காக்கிறது.\nமேற்கண்டவற்றுள் சரியானவை எவை?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "1, 2 மட்டும் சரி", "B": "அனைத்தும் சரி", "C": "2, 3 மட்டும் சரி", "D": "1, 3 மட்டும் சரி"}, "explanation": "திராவிட மொழிகள் ஒட்டுநிலை மொழிகள் (Agglutinative languages). வேர்ச்சொல்லுடன் விகுதிகள் சேரும் போது மூலப்பொருள் கெடாமல் நிற்கும். எனவே அனைத்துக் கூற்றுகளும் சரியானவை."}, "en": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "Analyze the common morphological characteristics of Dravidian languages:\n1. Most Dravidian languages are agglutinative in their morphological structure.\n2. Affixes and suffixes are suffixed sequentially to root bases to yield inflected meanings.\n3. Unlike inflected Indo-European tongues, the semantic integrity of the Dravidian root remains identifiable.\nWhich statements are correct?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "1 and 2 only are correct", "B": "All 1, 2, and 3 are correct", "C": "2 and 3 only are correct", "D": "1 and 3 only are correct"}, "explanation": "Agglutination and preserved root integrity are classic hallmarks of the Dravidian linguistic family."}}, "question_data": {"assertion": null, "reason": null, "statements": [], "matching_pairs": [], "or