{"id": "9th-u1-q048", "schema_version": "1.0", "kind": "direct", "level": "SSLC", "difficulty": "medium", "exam_mappings": ["group_4", "group_2", "group_2a"], "syllabus": {"class": "9", "subject_id": "general_tamil", "term": "full_year", "unit_id": "ta-9th-u1-mozhi", "lesson_id": "lesson-01-dravida-mozhi-kudumbam", "chapter_id": null, "topic_id": "topic-caldwell-biography", "subtopic_id": null}, "texts": {"ta": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "திராவிட மொழிகளின் ஒப்பிலக்கணத் தந்தை எனப் போற்றப்படும் ராபர்ட் கால்டுவெல் தமிழ்நாட்டில் தம் பெரும்பாலான ஆய்வுகளை மேற்கொண்ட இடம் எது?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "சாந்தோம் (சென்னை)", "B": "தஞ்சாவூர்", "C": "மதுரை", "D": "இடையன்குடி (திருநெல்வேலி)"}, "explanation": "ராபர்ட் கால்டுவெல் திருநெல்வேலி மாவட்டம் இடையன்குடியில் தங்கித் தமிழ் மக்களிடையே வாழ்ந்து தமது ஒப்பிலக்கண ஆய்வுகளை மேற்கொண்டார்."}, "en": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "In which historic town of Tamil Nadu did Bishop Robert Caldwell reside and accomplish the bulk of his monumental comparative Dravidian research?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "Santhome (Madras)", "B": "Thanjavur", "C": "Madurai", "D": "Idaiyangudi (Tirunelveli)"}, "explanation": "Bishop Caldwell lived and researched in Idaiyangudi in Tirunelveli district, where his memorial stands today."}}, "question_data": {"assertion": null, "reason": null, "statements": [], "matching_pairs": [], "ordered_items": [], "numeric_answer": null, "passage_reference": null, "table_reference": null, "image_reference": null}, "answer": {"correct_key": "D", "accepted_keys": ["D"], "correct_order": [], "matching_answer": [], "numeric_value": null, "explanation_key": null}, "question_settings": {"is_negative_question": false, "marks": 1.5, "negative_marks": 0.0, "allow_multiple_answers": false}, "source": {"type": "book", "book_name": "Tamil Nadu Samacheer Kalvi", "publisher": "Tamil Nadu Textbook and Educational Services Corporation", "class": "9", "term": "full_year", "edition": "2024-2025", "page": 5, "chapter": null, "section": null, "reference": "9th Tamil, Unit 1, Page 5", "url": null, "source_notes": null}, "previous_year": {"is_previous_year": false, "exam": null, "exam_name": null, "year": null, "paper": null, "session": null}, "media": {"has_media": false, "items": []}, "tags": ["caldwell", "idaiyangudi", "author_bio"], "language_status": {"ta": "available", "en": "available"}, "workflow": {"status": "published", "verification_status": "verified", "created_by": "admin", "created_at": "2026-11-04T09:50:00Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-04T09:50:00Z"}, "version": {"current": 1, "previous_version_id": null, "revision_reason": null}}
{"id": "9th-u1-q049", "schema_version": "1.0", "kind": "statement_analysis", "level": "SSLC", "difficulty": "medium", "exam_mappings": ["group_4", "group_2", "group_2a"], "syllabus": {"class": "9", "subject_id": "general_tamil", "term": "full_year", "unit_id": "ta-9th-u1-mozhi", "lesson_id": "lesson-01-dravida-mozhi-kudumbam", "chapter_id": null, "topic_id": "topic-linguistic-survey-india", "subtopic_id": null}, "texts": {"ta": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "இந்திய மொழிகள் குறித்த பின்வரும் புள்ளிவிவரக் கூற்றுகளை ஆராய்க:\n1. இந்திய நிலப்பரப்பில் பேசப்படும் மொழிகளின் எண்ணிக்கை 1300-க்கும் அதிகம் என மொழியியல் ஆய்வுகள் தெரிவிக்கின்றன.\n2. இவை இந்தோ-ஆசியன், திராவிடம், ஆஸ்ட்ரோ-ஆசியாடிக், சீன-திபெத்தியன் என நான்கு முதன்மைக் குடும்பங்களாகப் பிரிக்கப்பட்டுள்ளன.\n3. இந்திய மொழிகளில் திராவிட மொழிக் குடும்பமே எண்ணிக்கையில் மிகக் குறைவான மக்களைக் கொண்டதாகும்.\nமேற்கண்டவற்றுள் சரியான கூற்றுகள் எவை?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "1, 2 மட்டும் சரி", "B": "2, 3 மட்டும் சரி", "C": "1, 3 மட்டும் சரி", "D": "அனைத்தும் சரி"}, "explanation": "திராவிட மொழிக் குடும்பம் இந்தியாவில் இரண்டாவது மிகப்பெரிய மக்கள் தொகையினரால் பேசப்படும் குடும்பமாகும் (ஆஸ்ட்ரோ-ஆசியாடிக் மற்றும் சீன-திபெத்தியன் ஆகியவற்றை விட பன்மடங்கு பெரியது). எனவே கூற்று 3 தவறு; 1 மற்றும் 2 சரியானவை."}, "en": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "Examine the statistical statements concerning languages spoken in India:\n1. Over 1,300 languages and dialects are recognized across India.\n2. These belong fundamentally to four primary linguistic families: Indo-Asian, Dravidian, Austro-Asiatic, and Sino-Tibetan.\n3. The Dravidian family has the smallest speaker population among the four language families.\nWhich statements are correct?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "1 and 2 only are correct", "B": "2 and 3 only are correct", "C": "1 and 3 only are correct", "D": "All are correct"}, "explanation": "Dravidian is the second-largest linguistic family in India after Indo-Aryan. Statement 3 is false; 1 and 2 are correct."}}, "question_data": {"assertion": null, "reason": null, "statements": [], "matching_pairs": [], "ordered_items": [], "numeric_answer": null, "passage_reference": null, "table_reference": null, "image_reference": null}, "answer": {"correct_key": "A", "accepted_keys": ["A"], "correct_order": [], "matching_answer": [], "numeric_value": null, "explanation_key": null}, "question_settings": {"is_negative_question": false, "marks": 1.5, "negative_marks": 0.0, "allow_multiple_answers": false}, "source": {"type": "book", "book_name": "Tamil Nadu Samacheer Kalvi", "publisher": "Tamil Nadu Textbook and Educational Services Corporation", "class": "9", "term": "full_year", "edition": "2024-2025", "page": 4, "chapter": null, "section": null, "reference": "9th Tamil, Unit 1, Page 4", "url": null, "source_notes": null}, "previous_year": {"is_previous_year": false, "exam": null, "exam_name": null, "year": null, "paper": null, "session": null}, "media": {"has_media": false, "items": []}, "tags": ["linguistic_survey", "speaker_demographics", "statement_analysis"], "language_status": {"ta": "available", "en": "available"}, "workflow": {"status": "published", "verification_status": "verified", "created_by": "admin", "created_at": "2026-11-04T09:50:00Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-04T09:50:00Z"}, "version": {"current": 1, "previous_version_id": null, "revision_reason": null}}
{"id": "9th-u1-q050", "schema_version": "1.0", "kind": "assertion_reason", "level": "SSLC", "difficulty": "medium", "exam_mappings": ["group_4", "group_2", "group_2a"], "syllabus": {"class": "9", "subject_id": "general_tamil", "term": "full_year", "unit_id": "ta-9th-u1-mozhi", "lesson_id": "lesson-01-dravida-mozhi-kudumbam", "chapter_id": null, "topic_id": "topic-mangulam-inscriptions", "subtopic_id": null}, "texts": {"ta": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "கூற்று (A): திராவிட மொழிகளுள் தமிழின் கல்வெட்டுச் சான்றுகளே காலத்தால் முற்பட்டவையாக உள்ளன.\nகாரணம் (R): மதுரைக்கு அருகில் உள்ள மாங்குளம், அழகர்மலை ஆகியவற்றில் கண்டறியப்பட்ட தமிழ்-பிராமி கல்வெட்டுகள் கி.மு. 3-ஆம் நூற்றாண்டுக்குரியவை ஆகும்.", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "கூற்று (A) சரி, ஆனால் காரணம் (R) தவறு", "B": "கூற்று (A) மற்றும் காரணம் (R) இரண்டும் சரி; காரணம் கூற்றை விளக்குகிறது", "C": "கூற்று (A) தவறு, ஆனால் காரணம் (R) சரி", "D": "கூற்று (A) மற்றும் காரணம் (R) இரண்டும் தவறு"}, "explanation": "தமிழின் கல்வெட்டுகள் கி.மு. 3-ஆம் நூற்றாண்டைச் சேர்ந்தவை என்பதால் திராவிட மொழிகளிலேயே தமிழின் எழுத்துச் சான்றுகள் காலத்தால் மிகவும் முற்பட்டவை. கூற்று மற்றும் காரணம் இரண்டும் முற்றிலும் சரியானவை."}, "en": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "Assertion (A): Tamil possesses the earliest written epigraphical records among all Dravidian languages.\nReason (R): Tamil-Brahmi cave inscriptions found at sites like Mangulam and Alagarmalai near Madurai date firmly to the 3rd century BCE.", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "(A) is true, but (R) is false", "B": "Both (A) and (R) are true, and (R) correctly explains (A)", "C": "(A) is false, but (R) is true", "D": "Both (A) and (R) are false"}, "explanation": "Epigraphical evidence confirms Tamil's continuous epigraphical antiquity from 3rd century BCE. Both statements are accurate."}}, "question_data": {"assertion": null, "reason": null, "statements": [], "matching_pairs": [], "ordered_items": [], "numeric_answer": null, "passage_reference": null, "table_reference": null, "image_reference": null}, "answer": {"correct_key": "B", "accepted_keys": ["B"], "correct_order": [], "matching_answer": [], "numeric_value": null, "explanation_key": null}, "question_settings": {"is_negative_question": false, "marks": 1.5, "negative_marks": 0.0, "allow_multiple_answers": false}, "source": {"type": "book", "book_name": "Tamil Nadu Samacheer Kalvi", "publisher": "Tamil Nadu Textbook and Educational Services Corporation", "class": "9", "term": "full_year", "edition": "2024-2025", "page": 8, "chapter": null, "section": null, "reference": "9th Tamil, Unit 1, Page 8", "url": null, "source_notes": null}, "previous_year": {"is_previous_year": false, "exam": null, "exam_name": null, "year": null, "paper": null, "session": null}, "media": {"has_media": false, "items": []}, "tags": ["epigraphy", "mangulam", "assertion_reason"], "language_status": {"ta": "available", "en": "available"}, "workflow": {"status": "published", "verification_status": "verified", "created_by": "admin", "created_at": "2026-11-04T09:50:00Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-04T09:50:00Z"}, "version": {"current": 1, "previous_version_id": null, "revision_reason": null}}
{"id": "9th-u1-q051", "schema_version": "1.0", "kind": "matching", "level": "SSLC", "difficulty": "hard", "exam_mappings": ["group_4", "group_2", "group_2a"], "syllabus": {"class": "9", "subject_id": "general_tamil", "term": "full_year", "unit_id": "ta-9th-u1-mozhi", "lesson_id": "lesson-01-dravida-mozhi-kudumbam", "chapter_id": null, "topic_id": "topic-geographic-distribution", "subtopic_id": null}, "texts": {"ta": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "திராவிட மொழிக் குடும்பங்களையும் அவை பேசப்படும் முதன்மைப் புவியியல் பகுதிகளையும் பொருத்துக:\nபட்டியல் I:\na) தென் திராவிடம்\nb) நடு திராவிடம்\nc) வட திராவிடம் (பிராகுய்)\nd) வட திராவிடம் (மால்தோ)\n\nபட்டியல் II:\n1. பாகிஸ்தானின் பலுசிஸ்தான்\n2. ஜார்க்கண்ட் / மேற்கு வங்க ராஜ்மகால் குன்றுகள்\n3. தமிழ்நாடு, கேரளம், கர்நாடகம்\n4. ஆந்திரம், தெலங்கானா, மத்தியப் பிரதேசம்", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "a-4, b-3, c-1, d-2", "B": "a-3, b-4, c-2, d-1", "C": "a-3, b-4, c-1, d-2", "D": "a-1, b-2, c-3, d-4"}, "explanation": "தென் திராவிடம் = தமிழ்நாடு, கேரளம், கர்நாடகம் (3); நடு திராவிடம் = ஆந்திரம், தெலங்கானா, ம.பி. (4); பிராகுய் = பலுசிஸ்தான் (1); மால்தோ = ராஜ்மகால் குன்றுகள் (2). சரியான வரிசை: 3, 4, 1, 2."}, "en": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "Match the Dravidian sub-families/tongues with their geographic strongholds:\nList I: a) South Dravidian, b) Central Dravidian, c) North Dravidian (Brahui), d) North Dravidian (Malto)\nList II: 1. Balochistan (Pakistan), 2. Rajmahal Hills (Jharkhand/Bengal), 3. Tamil Nadu, Kerala & Karnataka, 4. Andhra, Telangana & Central India", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "a-4, b-3, c-1, d-2", "B": "a-3, b-4, c-2, d-1", "C": "a-3, b-4, c-1, d-2", "D": "a-1, b-2, c-3, d-4"}, "explanation": "South: TN/Kerala/Karnataka (3); Central: Andhra/Telangana (4); Brahui: Balochistan (1); Malto: Rajmahal Hills (2). Sequence: 3, 4, 1, 2."}}, "question_data": {"assertion": null, "reason": null, "statements": [], "matching_pairs": [], "ordered_items": [], "numeric_answer": null, "passage_reference": null, "table_reference": null, "image_reference": null}, "answer": {"correct_key": "C", "accepted_keys": ["C"], "correct_order": [], "matching_answer": [], "numeric_value": null, "explanation_key": null}, "question_settings": {"is_negative_question": false, "marks": 1.5, "negative_marks": 0.0, "allow_multiple_answers": false}, "source": {"type": "book", "book_name": "Tamil Nadu Samacheer Kalvi", "publisher": "Tamil Nadu Textbook and Educational Services Corporation", "class": "9", "term": "full_year", "edition": "2024-2025", "page": 6, "chapter": null, "section": null, "reference": "9th Tamil, Unit 1, Page 6", "url": null, "source_notes": null}, "previous_year": {"is_previous_year": false, "exam": null, "exam_name": null, "year": null, "paper": null, "session": null}, "media": {"has_media": false, "items": []}, "tags": ["geography", "matching", "dravidian_distribution"], "language_status": {"ta": "available", "en": "available"}, "workflow": {"status": "published", "verification_status": "verified", "created_by": "admin", "created_at": "2026-11-04T09:50:00Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-04T09:50:00Z"}, "version": {"current": 1, "previous_version_id": null, "revision_reason": null}}
{"id": "9th-u1-q052", "schema_version": "1.0", "kind": "direct", "level": "SSLC", "difficulty": "medium", "exam_mappings": ["group_4", "group_2", "group_2a"], "syllabus": {"class": "9", "subject_id": "general_tamil", "term": "full_year", "unit_id": "ta-9th-u1-mozhi", "lesson_id": "lesson-01-dravida-mozhi-kudumbam", "chapter_id": null, "topic_id": "topic-kavirajamarga-facts", "subtopic_id": null}, "texts": {"ta": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "கன்னட மொழியின் மிகத் தொன்மையான இலக்கிய நூலாகவும் இலக்கண நூலாகவும் ஒரே நேரத்தில் போற்றப்படும் நூல் எது?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "ஆந்திர பாஷா பூஷணம்", "B": "லீலாதிலகம்", "C": "ராமசரிதம்", "D": "கவிராஜமார்க்கம்"}, "explanation": "பாடநூல் பக். 8 அட்டவணையில்: கன்னடத்தின் இலக்கியம் மற்றும் இலக்கணம் ஆகிய இரண்டுக்குமே 'கவிராஜமார்க்கம்' (கி.பி. 9) என்ற ஒரே நூலே குறிப்பிடப்பட்டுள்ளது."}, "en": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "Which 9th-century text is uniquely cited in the textbook antiquity table as both the earliest literary work and the earliest grammar text for Kannada?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "Andhra Bhasha Bhushanam", "B": "Lilathilakam", "C": "Ramacharitam", "D": "Kavirajamarga"}, "explanation": "Kavirajamarga (9th century CE) serves as both the earliest literature and grammar source for Kannada."}}, "question_data": {"assertion": null, "reason": null, "statements": [], "matching_pairs": [], "ordered_items": [], "numeric_answer": null, "passage_reference": null, "table_reference": null, "image_reference": null}, "answer": {"correct_key": "D", "accepted_keys": ["D"], "correct_order": [], "matching_answer": [], "numeric_value": null, "explanation_key": null}, "question_settings": {"is_negative_question": false, "marks": 1.5, "negative_marks": 0.0, "allow_multiple_answers": false}, "source": {"type": "book", "book_name": "Tamil Nadu Samacheer Kalvi", "publisher": "Tamil Nadu Textbook and Educational Services Corporation", "class": "9", "term": "full_year", "edition": "2024-2025", "page": 8, "chapter": null, "section": null, "reference": "9th Tamil, Unit 1, Page 8", "url": null, "source_notes": null}, "previous_year": {"is_previous_year": false, "exam": null, "exam_name": null, "year": null, "paper": null, "session": null}, "media": {"has_media": false, "items": []}, "tags": ["kannada", "kavirajamarga", "direct_mcq"], "language_status": {"ta": "available", "en": "available"}, "workflow": {"status": "published", "verification_status": "verified", "created_by": "admin", "created_at": "2026-11-04T09:50:00Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-04T09:50:00Z"}, "version": {"current": 1, "previous_version_id": null, "revision_reason": null}}
{"id": "9th-u1-q053", "schema_version": "1.0", "kind": "statement_analysis", "level": "SSLC", "difficulty": "medium", "exam_mappings": ["group_4", "group_2", "group_2a"], "syllabus": {"class": "9", "subject_id": "general_tamil", "term": "full_year", "unit_id": "ta-9th-u1-mozhi", "lesson_id": "lesson-01-dravida-mozhi-kudumbam", "chapter_id": null, "topic_id": "topic-moolachol-porutham", "subtopic_id": null}, "texts": {"ta": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "திராவிட மொழிகளின் சொல் ஒற்றுமை குறித்த பின்வரும் இணைகளை ஆராய்க:\n1. மரம் - தமிழ் மற்றும் மலையாளத்தில் ஒரே வடிவைக் கொண்டுள்ளது.\n2. கண் - தமிழ், மலையாளம், கன்னடம், தெலுங்கு, குடகு ஆகிய அனைத்திலும் 'கண்/கண்ணு' என்றே வேர்ச்சொல் அமைகிறது.\n3. மூன்று - துளு மொழியில் 'மூறு' என வழங்குகிறது.\nமேற்கண்டவற்றுள் சரியான இணைகள் எவை?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "1, 2 மட்டும் சரி", "B": "2, 3 மட்டும் சரி", "C": "1, 3 மட்டும் சரி", "D": "அனைத்தும் சரி"}, "explanation": "துளு மொழியில் 'மூன்று' என்பது 'மூஜி' என வழங்குகிறது ('மூறு' என்பது கன்னடத்தில் வழங்குகிறது). எனவே கூற்று 3 தவறு; 1 மற்றும் 2 சரியானவை."}, "en": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "Examine the statements regarding lexical cognates across Dravidian languages:\n1. 'Maram' shares an identical phonetic shape in both Tamil and Malayalam.\n2. The root for eye ('Kan/Kannu') is shared identically across Tamil, Malayalam, Kannada, Telugu, and Kodagu.\n3. The numeral 'Three' is pronounced as 'Mooru' in Tulu.\nWhich statements are correct?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "1 and 2 only are correct", "B": "2 and 3 only are correct", "C": "1 and 3 only are correct", "D": "All are correct"}, "explanation": "In Tulu, three is 'Mooji' ('Mooru' is in Kannada). Statements 1 and 2 are correct."}}, "question_data": {"assertion": null, "reason": null, "statements": [], "matching_pairs": [], "ordered_items": [], "numeric_answer": null, "passage_reference": null, "table_reference": null, "image_reference": null}, "answer": {"correct_key": "A", "accepted_keys": ["A"], "correct_order": [], "matching_answer": [], "numeric_value": null, "explanation_key": null}, "question_settings": {"is_negative_question": false, "marks": 1.5, "negative_marks": 0.0, "allow_multiple_answers": false}, "source": {"type": "book", "book_name": "Tamil Nadu Samacheer Kalvi", "publisher": "Tamil Nadu Textbook and Educational Services Corporation", "class": "9", "term": "full_year", "edition": "2024-2025", "page": 6, "chapter": null, "section": null, "reference": "9th Tamil, Unit 1, Page 6", "url": null, "source_notes": null}, "previous_year": {"is_previous_year": false, "exam": null, "exam_name": null, "year": null, "paper": null, "session": null}, "media": {"has_media": false, "items": []}, "tags": ["lexical_cognates", "tulu_numerals", "statement_analysis"], "language_status": {"ta": "available", "en": "available"}, "workflow": {"status": "published", "verification_status": "verified", "created_by": "admin", "created_at": "2026-11-04T09:50:00Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-04T09:50:00Z"}, "version": {"current": 1, "previous_version_id": null, "revision_reason": null}}
{"id": "9th-u1-q054", "schema_version": "1.0", "kind": "direct", "level": "SSLC", "difficulty": "easy", "exam_mappings": ["group_4", "group_2", "group_2a"], "syllabus": {"class": "9", "subject_id": "general_tamil", "term": "full_year", "unit_id": "ta-9th-u1-mozhi", "lesson_id": "lesson-01-dravida-mozhi-kudumbam", "chapter_id": null, "topic_id": "topic-oppilakkana-thanthai", "subtopic_id": null}, "texts": {"ta": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "'திராவிட மொழிகளின் ஒப்பிலக்கணத் தந்தை' என்று தமிழ்நாடு முழுமையாலும் போற்றப்படும் அறிஞர் யார்?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "ஜி.யு. போப்", "B": "ராபர்ட் கால்டுவெல்", "C": "பிரான்சிஸ் எல்லிஸ்", "D": "வீரமாமுனிவர்"}, "explanation": "1856-இல் வெளியான 'திராவிட மொழிகளின் ஒப்பிலக்கணம்' நூலின் மூலம் திராவிட மொழிக் குடும்பத்தின் தனித்தன்மையை உலகுக்கு நிலைநாட்டிய ராபர்ட் கால்டுவெல் 'திராவிட ஒப்பிலக்கணத் தந்தை' எனப் போற்றப்படுகிறார்."}, "en": {"blocks": [{"type": "text", "content": "Who is widely honored as the 'Father of Comparative Dravidian Linguistics'?", "media_id": null}], "options": {"A": "Rev. G.U. Pope", "B": "Dr. Robert Caldwell", "C": "Francis Whyte Ellis", "D": "Constanzo Beschi"}, "explanation": "Dr. Robert Caldwell is universally celebrated as the Father of Comparative Dravidian Linguistics for his monumental 1856 treatise."}}, "question_data": {"assertion": null, "reason": null, "statements": [], "matching_pairs": [], "ordered_items": [], "numeric_answer": null, "passage_reference": null, "table_reference": null, "image_reference": null}, "answer": {"correct_key": "B", "accepted_keys": ["B"], "correct_order": [], "matching_answer": [], "numeric_value": null, "explanation_key": null}, "question_settings": {"is_negative_question": false, "marks": 1.5, "negative_marks": 0.0, "allow_multiple_answers": false}, "source": {"type": "book", "book_name": "Tamil Nadu Samacheer Kalvi", "publisher": "Tamil Nadu Textbook and Educational Services Corporation", "class": "9", "term": "full_year", "edition": "2024-2025", "